WEBVTT

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.320
<b>Master of the Island</b>

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.990
<i>The rescue team hasn't come yet.</i>

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.450
<i>To be honest, I'm super worried.</i>

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.780
That's looking pretty good!

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.700
There's no roof yet,
so there's still a ways to go.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.250
<i>We only have this water thanks to her.</i>

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.380
<i>I mean, it is rain water though.</i>

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.010
<i>She's become master of this island...</i>

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.130
<i>Onishima Homare.</i>

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.970
Homare! I'm hungry...

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.310
We've been working on this since
morning and we've only gotten this far.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.560
You all take breaks as soon as we start.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.440
<i>She's always got this cold attitude,</i>

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.400
<i>but when I threw a tantrum,
she went and found food for us.</i>

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.820
Sea urchin                              Cicadas        Seaweed

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.820
Mysterious jar

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.620
I'm so hungry I can't move anymore!

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.290
Once we finish the roof.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:05.580
I don't wanna! I don't wanna! I'm starving!

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.580
You don't find that embarrassing?

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.670
Asuka-san... you're slacking
off and behaving like this?

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.510
Don't look at me like that!

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.430
We don't have enough vines...

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.090
I'm going into the forest.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.050
Okay! Right! I'll go, too!

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:20.970
I'll help!

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:25.560
<i>If something seems edible,
I can just have Homare check it out!</i>

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.140
<i>I'm so smart!</i>

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:37.690
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:40.490
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.210
Hey! Aren't those taro leaves?

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.380
I've seen them in my grandma's field!

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:41.090
They do seem like potato leaves, however...

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.390
Right? Right?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.300
Let's try digging them up.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.260
Yay!

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.310
It might look right, but there's a similar
plant, giant elephant ear, with no tubers.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.310
Potato! Potato!

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.140
Seriously?

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.240
Yes! It has a potato! We have a taro!

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.110
That is obviously not a taro.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:05.410
Tubers are tubers.
I wonder if I can eat it raw.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.790
Don't do it. You shouldn't
eat things you're not sure about.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:09.910
Huh?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.210
It's a potato.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.420
Just a potato.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.460
Hey, you're a potato, right?

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.380
Yes.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.010
See?

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.720
I do see. It's very sad.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.640
<i>What's with her?</i>

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.760
<i>It's a potato.</i>

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.970
<i>She thinks bugs are edible,
so why are potatoes bad?</i>

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.730
Asuka, you should give up the idea of—

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:34.810
I don't wanna! I'm sure you can eat this!

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.940
If you're that insistent,
shall we try a patch test?

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.240
What's that?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:47.620
<b>Jouichi</b>

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:47.620
<b>Survival Training</b>

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:47.620
<b>Patch Test</b>

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.950
In this case, a patch test
can also be called an edibility test.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.620
An edibility test?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:51.620
You're testing an unknown to
see if it's harmful, without eating it.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.500
You apply a cut surface to your
skin and observe the reaction.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.250
Oh, I see!

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.130
That's how it works.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.630
Wow...

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.880
Now, where should we test it...

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.640
How about our bottoms?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.600
Come on. Come on!

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.310
All right.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.390
Be gent—

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.140
After about 15 minutes we'll—

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.140
Homare.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.820
My bottom's already starting
to feel tingly and numb.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.230
How's it looking?

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:22.820
This looks like poison.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.240
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.240
The night-scented lily 
contains calcium oxalate
 which irritates the skin.
 If accidentally ingested,
 it can cause paralysis and...

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.740
Really?

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.540
Weren't you going to help?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.120
I can't really take any more.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.920
Please let me lie here.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.800
<i>This is bad. I'm so hungry my hands are shak—</i>

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:45.930
<i>A cicada.</i>

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.050
<i>Homare ate one of these, right?</i>

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.270
Stop it! Stop it! Stop scrabbling around!

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.900
I can't do it! I just can't! It's scary!

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.190
That's such a waste.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.940
It almost got away.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.030
The neck area is good.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.240
It's like shrimp, right?

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.870
It might be kind of good.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.830
<i>There's no mistake.</i>

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.300
<i>This girl really is... the master of this island!</i>

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.510
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.670
Really?

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.470
<i>Everyone must be worried now.</i>

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:31.930
<i>Father, Mother...</i>

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.350
<i>Arnold, are you all right?</i>

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:41.360
<i>I'm sure they could never
imagine me sipping rainwater...</i>

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:48.280
<i>Here, there are no cold beverages,
delicious foods, or soft pets.</i>

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.660
The shelter's pretty much done, huh?

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.080
Everyone!

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.540
After the shelter's done,
we need a shower next.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.920
The order of priorities is body
temperature, water, food,

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.670
so wouldn't the next thing we need be food?

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.970
I do understand that, but...

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:12.510
we're all waiting for rescue, aren't we?

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:15.720
If and when the rescue team 
does come, they think,

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.190
"Yuck, these girls stink of sweat."

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:22.150
If they thought that, I just wouldn't
be able to live! Would you?

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:26.490
A shower. Hmm...

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.530
<b>Please. Please.                             Please!</b>

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.410
Let's give it a try.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.620
Hygiene and survival are connected after all.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.990
Yay! Thank you, Homare-san!

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.040
Warm water, if possible!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.330
Warm water, huh?

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.670
Done.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:42.840
It's a shower.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.590
What?

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.670
I used a plastic sheet I found
on the beach to hold the water.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.140
The flexibility of the branch allows
you to control the water flow.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.640
U-Umm...

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.680
Isn't the view a little too unobstructed here?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.770
If the sun can't get to it,
the water won't be warm.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.810
Isn't that great, Shion?

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.320
Please, you should use it first!

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.780
Wh-What...?

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.780
<i>Being naked in a place like this, outside...</i>

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.610
<i>It feels amazing!</i>

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.580
<i>It is a deserted island after all. So, why not?</i>

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.160
How is it, Shion?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.960
Is the water warm?

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.670
Yes. Very.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.800
<i>And you're way too close!</i>

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.050
This is pretty hard to control.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:31.840
<i>I'm so embarrassed I could die...</i>

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:37.970
<i>Father, Mother, Arnold.</i>

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.680
<i>I'm doing just fine!</i>

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.940
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.190
Is that so?

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:51.950
Food you can get from the ocean...
Would that be shellfish and things?

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.950
Since we only have our bare hands, yes.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:58.740
<i>The things I learned in school
are of no use here on this island.</i>

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.250
<i>But there's a teacher
here on this island, too.</i>

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.870
<i>A teacher named Onishima Homare.</i>

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.590
Let's try here.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.210
We can get things here?

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.340
It's more efficient than digging in the sand.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:14.840
What? Are you going in the water?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.810
<i>Homare-san just strips
without any hesitation.</i>

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:22.270
Having your assistance is a great help,
but you don't need to force yourself.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:25.690
Oh, no. I'm not forcing myself at all!

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:26.940
I see.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.610
In that case, will you get ready, too, Mutsu?

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:33.280
Of course! I'll take off my clothes in a flash.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.580
<i>Those who do not work should not eat.</i>

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.410
<i>I'm doing this!</i>

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:42.790
Just the bottoms

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.500
Shellfish cling to the rocks.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.790
It's hard to see them through
the reflections on the water,

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.010
so use your own shadow 
to see through the water.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.090
All right!

00:08:58.550 --> 00:08:59.890
Homare-san!

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.060
What about this one?

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.480
Oh, that's a whelk.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.190
Don't worry. It's edible.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:09.110
Okay!

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.610
We got quite a few!

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.490
They're moving!

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.750
Oh, it's a hermit crab. How cute!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.870
I picked you up by accident. Sorry!

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.340
What are you doing?

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.920
There was a hermit crab
mixed in, so I let it go.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:39.850
I actually like hermit crabs more, but...

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:43.270
What? You can eat hermit crabs?

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:44.980
<b>Glare</b>

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:44.890
I'm sorry.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:50.480
<i>It seems harsh, but by eating
you I'll be able to live.</i>

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.690
Watch. It's this part inside that tastes good.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.240
Oh. I... I'm really looking
forward to tasting it!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.030
<i>It's so harsh! It really is!</i>

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:04.040
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.240
Is that so?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.210
Welcome back!

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.420
What did you find?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.880
We collected lots of shellfish!

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.630
I'll make a fire.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.800
A fire? How?

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.420
Well...

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:24.390
I'll use a bottle filled with
water as a convex lens.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:29.770
Add dried leaves that will
serve as a fire starter...

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:31.520
and if you wave them gently...

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.150
That's amazing...

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.610
It takes a while for the stone to heat up,

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.320
but it makes it easier to cook
things all the way through.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.950
It feels like the first time
since we came to this island

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.120
that I'm seeing food a human
would actually eat!

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.370
We don't know how it tastes yet.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.380
How are we supposed to eat these?

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:53.290
The same as you would
a regular conch or snail.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.380
Use a slender stick to stab
the meat, give it a twist, and...

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.590
It's good, right? Given those faces!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:05.810
It's like eating a tiny turban shell!

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.770
What is this? It really is delicious!

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:09.560
Right?

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.480
Hold on, we're all eating too much.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.400
There won't be any left for Homare-san.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:18.070
It's all right. There's still
hermit crab for dessert.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.490
Sh-Shion-san?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.740
Shion-san!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.600
Next time, Case 4: "Trap."

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.750
<b>Trap</b>

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.750
<b></b>
